<p>UK Cabinet Office minister Josh Simons has resigned after scrutiny over his conduct before he was elected as an MP, including a probe involving journalists, according to the Financial Times. The Guardian said Simons came under pressure after it reported that he falsely linked reporters to a “pro-Kremlin” network in emails to GCHQ. That followed earlier comments in which Simons said he was “surprised” and “furious” about a PR firm’s investigation into journalists’ work. Simons said he resigned because his role in government had become “a distraction from this government’s important work”.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Timing: Simons resigned on Saturday after mounting pressure, the Guardian reported.</li><li>Political backdrop: The resignation comes after Labour placed third in a “crunch” by-election on Feb 26, according to the Straits Times.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Josh Simons: He resigned, saying his position in office had become “a distraction from this government’s important work.” (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/feb/28/minister-josh-simons-resigns-labour-together'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Starmer’s ethics adviser: The adviser warned of “potential reputational damage” from Simons’ pre-election activities, adding scrutiny to his conduct before he became an MP. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/213eb2fb-3dca-4795-b535-f940090e17fd'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>The Guardian (reporting): It said Simons previously ran the thinktank Labour Together, which has faced scrutiny in reporting over commissioning a PR firm to investigate journalists. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/feb/28/minister-josh-simons-resigns-labour-together'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/213eb2fb-3dca-4795-b535-f940090e17fd'>Labour minister quits over probe into journalists</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/feb/28/minister-josh-simons-resigns-labour-together'>Labour minister Josh Simons resigns after falsely linking journalists to ‘pro-Kremlin’ network</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/british-pm-starmer-dealt-new-setback-as-another-minister-resigns'>British PM Starmer dealt new setback as another minister resigns</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>